{
  "comment": "Same plugin-panel pattern as the D-110/JV layouts. The TONE being edited is picked with the program selector (banks T1x-T4x = the 32 RAM tones); picking one only moves the edit target, nothing is sent (see s330.json driverNotes 1). Rows follow the S-330 signal path: wave (points/loop of the sample in RAM) + pitch -> TVF + its 8-stage envelope -> TVA envelope, LFO (one LFO, three depths) and velocity -> patch P11 / voice group A context. Envelopes are 8 level/rate pairs with a sustain point and end point, not DADSR, so each envelope group has a stage select (1-8) over one level + one rate knob. Wave points are 24-bit sample indices relative to the tone's first segment; loop length must follow end - loop (driverNotes 4). The patch group edits P11 (the patch voice group A plays by factory default): its tone-to-key map is per key (109 keys x 2 layers), so three picks show layer 1 at C2/C4/C6 rather than a key range.",
